{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>אל נא.</b> Genesis 20:13 — and I have already informed you of the grammar of the nagid [word]." "<b>כראות פני אלהים.</b> An angel. And most of the commentators say that the angel came to Jacob to strengthen his heart so that he would not fear his brother, for behold, the angel could not prevail against him, though he was a human being. And the word שרית עם אלהים is not like 'וישר אבימלך על ישראל' (Judges 9:22), for עם is not like על; rather, its meaning is 'you are accounted a prince among the angels,' and if people, 'among people.' And they will ask: what is the meaning of 'ויזרח לו השמש' (the sun rose for him)? Does it not rise over the entire world in a single instant? Their question is void, for the time the sun rises changes in every place. Between Jerusalem and this city in which I composed this commentary — its name is Lucca — there is an hour and a third of an hour, and a span of twelve degrees, and this matter is clear without any doubt. And the meaning of והוא צולע is that he walked on his one side. And the meaning of על כן לדבר is as explained."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:56.175013691Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}